      "writtenOn": "2022-12-21T22:26:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is there ever a case when an application would intentionally want us to report a smaller MTU than what we actually have (e.g. for interop reasons)?\n\nAlso, then should we remove the Java API entirely and just immediately request a large MTU on connection?",
      "revId": "e4dbc443c8d963e813ee04129b1242f7fa4e60cd",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ce58647c_68d9a1cf",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1958203
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-12-21T22:26:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "(unresolved)",
      "parentUuid": "cff7553f_d24be091",
      "revId": "e4dbc443c8d963e813ee04129b1242f7fa4e60cd",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5de72b18_5f127cb0",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1958203
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-12-21T22:28:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "To me a safer change would be to allow only the first application to set whatever MTU it wants, and then subsequent requests would be rejected.\n\nAnd then, for LE Audio devices / devices with BT profiles, we as the stack would be the first application to request a large MTU. So for 3P peripherals used by only one app (which is the common case) we don\u0027t have to worry.",
      "parentUuid": "ce58647c_68d9a1cf",
      "revId": "e4dbc443c8d963e813ee04129b1242f7fa4e60cd",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3b27ae27_2f46946f",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1929540
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-12-21T22:57:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Unfortunately proposed solutions just introduce races because it is not assured that LeAudio code will do ask for MTU first.\n\nMTU is the stack thing and valid question is why it was exposed up to the Java developers at all. Especially that it can be done only once.\nI already faced couple of issues related to this.\n\nI\u0027m pretty confident about us having this solution.",
      "parentUuid": "5de72b18_5f127cb0",
      "revId": "e4dbc443c8d963e813ee04129b1242f7fa4e60cd",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a4491c89_498ac227",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 5
